Union-Find that silently splits components — a classic linking blunder. Put this in dsu.py as-is:

class DSU:
    def __init__(self, n):
        self.p = list(range(n))
    def find(self, x):
        while self.p[x] != x:
            self.p[x] = self.p[self.p[x]]
            x = self.p[x]
        return x
    def union(self, a, b):
        if self.find(a) == self.find(b):
            return False
        self.p[b] = a
        return True
    def connected(self, a, b):
        return self.find(a) == self.find(b)

The bug: union links ELEMENT b instead of b's root. Write test_dsu.py that proves it with a three-union sequence where a previously-connected pair reports disconnected (hint: union(0, 1), then union(2, 1), then check 0 and 1), run pytest and show the failure. Fix union to link roots, add union-by-size while you are in there, then fuzz: 2000 seeded random unions on 200 elements mirrored against a naive label-propagation oracle, checking connected() on 50 random pairs after every 100 ops. Everything green before you finish.

